====== Sagem F@ST2504n v.6======

The Sagem F@ST2504n router used to be distributed by Sky to their UK broadband customers.

{{section>meta:infobox:broadcom_wifi#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

{{section>meta:infobox:broadcom_dsl#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

{{:meta:icons:tango:48px-dialog-warning.svg.png?nolink&24 | Warning }}
DO NOT flash OpenWrt if you intend to go back to the stock Sky firmware.
The customer-specific configuration is lost when erasing the flash,
so if you intend to ever use it with Sky again, consult
the user forums on how to use a third-party router with the Sky service first.

| FIXME To be confirmed. |

(Still to be confirmed, but the end of the stock flash layout contains "PSI" blocks, which should be required for PPPoE access to Sky Broadband. OpenWRT overwrites the end of the flash with the JFFS2 filesystem.)



